  "content": {
    "id": "v2-c147d-p51-practice-slot-5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Find, using the Pythagorean identity:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "v2-c147d-p51-practice-slot-5-s5-q-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$$\\int_0^{\\pi/6}\\cos^3 x\\,dx$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{11}{24}$",
          "worked": "$$\\cos^3 x=\\cos x(1-\\sin^2 x)$$\n$$\\int_0^{\\pi/6}\\cos^3 x\\,dx=\\int_0^{\\pi/6}\\cos x(1-\\sin^2 x)\\,dx$$\nLet $u=\\sin x$, so $du=\\cos x\\,dx$.\n\nThe limits become $u=0$ when $x=0$, and $u=\\frac12$ when $x=\\frac\\pi6$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\int_0^{\\pi/6}\\cos^3 x\\,dx&=\\int_0^{1/2}(1-u^2)\\,du\\\\&=\\left[u-\\frac{u^3}{3}\\right]_0^{1/2}\\\\&=\\frac12-\\frac1{24}\\\\&=\\frac{11}{24}.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "v2-c147d-p51-practice-slot-5-s5-q-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$$\\int\\sin^2 x\\cos^3 x\\,dx$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac13\\sin^3 x-\\frac15\\sin^5 x+C$",
          "worked": "$$\\sin^2 x\\cos^3 x=\\sin^2 x\\cos x(1-\\sin^2 x)$$\nLet $u=\\sin x$, so $du=\\cos x\\,dx$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\int\\sin^2 x\\cos^3 x\\,dx&=\\int u^2(1-u^2)\\,du\\\\&=\\int(u^2-u^4)\\,du\\\\&=\\frac{u^3}{3}-\\frac{u^5}{5}+C\\\\&=\\frac13\\sin^3 x-\\frac15\\sin^5 x+C.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      }
    ]
  },
